From ef1271af635791c8c0bf0878b89cae8bdab2198d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 23:29:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Log the TPM's banks and append the PSP's TCG log

The event log declared SHA-1 and SHA-256 whatever banks the TPM had,
and Linux resets on a log whose banks differ from the TPM's: its extend
wants one digest per allocated bank, in the TPM's order. Ask the TPM for
its PCR allocation with TPM2_GetCapability and declare exactly those
banks in that order. Each record carries SHA-1 and SHA-256 where the TPM
has them and the TCG placeholder digest, one then zeros, elsewhere,
which is extended into that bank as well so the log replays there. A
TPM that does not answer, one behind a locked locality among them, is
taken for the SHA-1 and SHA-256 one a discrete TPM ships as.

Under the PSP DRTM service the extends of PCR 17 and 18 between SKINIT
and the DLME are the service's, kept in a log of its own, so the log the
DLME found could not replay to the PCRs. The AMDSL SKL now fetches that
log with DRTM_CMD_GET_TCG_LOGS after the OSSL extend and appends its
records, bar the SKINIT one it logged already, rewritten to the log's
banks: a digest the record carries for a bank is kept, a bank it lacks
gets the placeholder and the extend. Its log starts after the launch,
at the locality the service unlocks with it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
